 3. 🤖 AI tensions surface at summit 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg speaks virtually at the G20 innovation summit yesterday in Chapel Hill, N.C. Photo: Matt Ramey/AFP via Getty Images Axios' Maria Curi writes from the G20 innovation summit in Chapel Hill, N.C.: 

 Trump administration officials came to this week's innovation summit to project a united front on U.S. AI leadership. But tensions between the Commerce Department and the White House's tech policy shop are playing out behind the scenes.

 Why it matters: The Trump administration wants the world to follow its lead on AI policy, even as it grapples with divisions at home. The two-day G20 Innovation Ministerial, which culminates today, features some of the tech industry's heaviest hitters and officials from the world's most powerful countries.

 Officials and executives pitched the U.S. as a model for other countries on AI, contrasting its lighter regulatory approach with the European Union's heavier hand. 🔭 Between the lines: The Commerce Department and OSTP are jockeying for control over the administration's AI policy agenda as key regulatory decisions remain unsettled.

 Commerce holds many of the administration's most important AI policy levers, including the Bureau of Industry and Security and the Center for AI Standards and Innovation. Keep reading . 

 
 
