 7. ⚖️ Death penalty resurgence 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Death Penalty Information Center. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals Florida yesterday executed its 14th prisoner this year, adding to a post-COVID surge in capital punishment that drove more executions last year than any year since 2009, Axios' Avery Lotz writes. 

 Even as fewer courts sentence defendants to death and more than half of the states have banned or at least temporarily halted the practice, the Trump administration has overtly cheered on the death penalty. By the numbers: 47 people were executed last year, 19 in Florida.

 24 people have been executed this year, with 10 more scheduled. Keep reading . 

 
 
