 8. 🎓 1 for the road: Campus robot wars 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A new cohort of fresh-faced delivery robots is arriving on college campuses this fall after the leading incumbent left the market, Axios Future of Mobility author Joann Muller writes. 

 Why it matters: College students are a surprisingly good test audience for delivery robots. They're hungry at weird hours, impatient, tech-friendly — and live in a compact environment where walking 15 minutes for dinner can feel like an intolerable burden. Starship Technologies, which pioneered college robot delivery, announced in May it was shifting its U.S. focus to more lucrative grocery deliveries.

 Universities accustomed to the roving robots moved swiftly to recruit replacements. Avride operated robots on four campuses last year. Now it's adding 21 that were previously served by Starship. Robot.com just signed a seven-year agreement with food service company Sodexo. Keep reading . 

 
 
